/*
!.gitignore

# `/*` rather than `*`: a bare `*` matches at every depth, so it kept matching
# the files *inside* brand/ and img/ and no directory-level negation could undo
# it. Scoped to the immediate children it ignores the build output (css/, js/,
# icons/) while letting git descend into the two source directories.
#
# The root .gitignore documents brand/ and img/ as *source*, not build output:
# nothing in `npm run build` produces the logo, the OG cards or the payment
# method marks. Without these negations this file won over the root rules and
# every one of those files existed only on the machine that generated it.
!brand/
!img/
